# Methods generator

Choose the microscope and hardware you used to build a draft microscopy methods paragraph, then add your acquisition settings and review the text before publication. The draft follows the **QUAREP-LiMi minimal reporting recommendations** for light microscopy ([Better reporting is better science](https://rupress.org/jcb/article/225/3/e202601032/281525/Better-reporting-is-better-science-Community)).

!!! tip "Generate the draft when you acquire the images"
    The generator reflects the facility record available now; it does not reconstruct earlier microscope configurations. We therefore recommend generating and saving the Methods draft at the time of image acquisition, together with the raw image metadata. Historical configuration support can be added later when the repository has an explicit time-versioned configuration model.

