### Recover acquisition settings from image metadata

Exact exposure times, pixel size, z-step, laser settings, and other acquisition parameters are often stored in the original image metadata. In Fiji/ImageJ, open the raw file and use **Image > Show Info...** (or press **I**) to inspect the metadata. Copy the relevant values into your records. If you use an assistant to extract fields from metadata text, verify every value against the raw metadata before publication.

### Generated methods draft

**Add to methods** commits the acquisition you have described. Correcting a selection and adding again updates that same entry rather than duplicating it; **Start another acquisition** clears every selection and starts a separate entry. A new acquisition reference, or changing the imaging method, also starts a separate entry and clears the hardware selections, keeping only the imaging method so you can correct it. **Clear all** empties the draft and every selection, including the confirmed actions and any reviewed Virtual Microscope plan. Save the draft with the acquisition records while the selected configuration is current. Finished Methods prose is kept separate from a **Review before publication** block listing every acquisition detail that still needs to be specified or verified; requests that apply to the whole section are stated once at the end rather than repeated under every acquisition.
